(THG2-31: a field always wins over a function of the same name, because the
 collision rule refuses the program rather than letting one shadow the other.
 The type owns one member space, so a global function whose first parameter is
 a point cannot be called `x` when point already has a field `x`.
 LANGUAGE.md:1712-1717, verbatim.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox THG2-31.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: point already has a field called 'x', so a function taking a point cannot be called 'x' too
   followed by "Rename one of the two - Vox refuses the ambiguity rather than
   choosing between them." No binary is produced; this is a compile error.
)
